  "sunTime": "Sun time",
  "aboutBody": "Sun Clock divides the day into 24 hours that follow the sun. Sunrise is always 06:00 and sunset always 18:00. The 12 day hours share the real daylight evenly, and the 12 night hours share the night.\n\nIn winter, day hours are short and night hours long; in summer it is the other way round. At the equinoxes every hour is close to 60 minutes.\n\nSunrise and sunset are calculated with the NOAA solar formulas (the upper edge of the sun touching the horizon, with standard refraction). When the sun does not rise or set at all, the clock shows apparent solar time, with 12:00 at solar noon.",
